  slug: "herdr-core-helper",
  title: "Herdr Core Helper",
  description: "A small command-line helper for herdr core terminals, wrapping its `hc` command. `hch where` shows the space, tab and pane the current terminal is in. `hch version` compares the herdr core build the tab is running with the one installed. `hch up` swaps the tab's shell for a fresh one on the installed build, in the same tab and folder, so an update takes effect without rebuilding the layout.",

  tagline: "Little helpers for herdr core.",
  motivation: "These started as zsh functions in my dotfiles. As they grew, I wanted them tested and in one place rather than as jq pipelines in an alias file, and easy for other herdr core users to install and use too.",
